    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nI'd like to have a wide preview when I'm previewing a source code file but when I'm previewing a directory I would prefer if it used the default unfocused width. What I would like is to be able to pass a function to width_preview so I can configure it based on preview type but I'm not sure if there's a way to do this already.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, it would be nice to only enable preview on leaf nodes.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.files</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd like to have a wide preview when I'm previewing a source code file but when I'm previewing a directory I would prefer if it used the default unfocused width. What I would like is to be able to pass a function to width_preview so I can configure it based on preview type but I'm not sure if there's a way to do this already.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Alternatively, it would be nice to only enable preview on leaf nodes.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.files\nQuestion\nI'd like to have a wide preview when I'm previewing a source code file but when I'm previewing a directory I would prefer if it used the default unfocused width. What I would like is to be able to pass a function to width_preview so I can configure it based on preview type but I'm not sure if there's a way to do this already.\nAlternatively, it would be nice to only enable preview on leaf nodes.",
